+### 12.3.10 Bounded environment embedded-pip extraction failures (R07-C D-M-E)
+
+For `env.llm_critical_deps_pinned` only, independently opt the existing
+`environment.yml` / `environment.yaml` embedded-pip extraction call into the
+internal `unparsed_requirement` fact introduced by §12.3.9. This records failed
+extraction by the current Requirement parser, not invalid pip syntax, an invalid
+Conda environment, a failed installation or complete manager validation.
+
+Limit the trigger to a string actually traversed in the existing decoded
+`dependencies` list, inside a mapping entry whose existing `pip` value is a list.
+Keep the current `isinstance(pip_line, str) and pip_line.strip()` guard and the
+existing stripped argument to `_add_requirement_line`. Missing keys, empty lists,
+empty/whitespace-only strings and skipped non-string members do not themselves
+create this cause. Existing bounded structure failures remain separate.
+
+Only an already-caught failure of that exact existing Requirement call creates
+the fact; record it from the helper's existing result, not diagnostic prose.
+Do not add parsing, normalize differently, pre-scan, retry or repair a string,
+strip comments, expand a directive/include, follow a URL/path, read another file
+or execute pip/Conda/a solver. Successfully parsed strings retain all existing
+semantics. In particular the graph-only D-C fallback is not extended here.
+Supported Conda strings and unknown installer/selector mappings retain their
+existing behavior and are not newly diagnosed by this trigger.
+
+Record at most one `unparsed_requirement` per logical source path using the
+existing dictionary. Preserve any earlier `unreadable`, `invalid_syntax` or
+`invalid_structure` instead of overwriting it; structure checks already precede
+extraction for the whole decoded document. Keep default-empty legacy/manual
+internal values and add no persisted schema field or new reason vocabulary.
+
+Preserve every partial declaration, order, canonical name, specifier, exact
+version, logical source and existing line value. The environment extractor's
+line value is the one-based outer `dependencies` entry ordinal, shared by all
+pip members of that entry; this policy does not convert it to a YAML physical
+line or add per-entry evidence. Existing diagnostics continue to use the
+original stripped parse argument and this ordinal without new diagnostic text.
+Preserve reads, discovery and budgets, manifest/lock presence, qualified project
+roots, uncertain-directory barriers and all format-lock packages/associations,
+including same-directory environment ambiguity and existing Conda exact credit.
+An extraction failure adds no ownership barrier and grants or revokes no credit.
+
+Reuse §12.3.6's unchanged declaration-failure consumption, message, hint and
+file-level evidence. Exact or qualified credit wins first, then D-F/D-S, then
+D-L, then nonempty declaration failures (including this trigger), then D-G.
+Preserve earlier branches' full findings and per-package iteration. A new path
+can enlarge sorted D-M evidence even if the status was already SKIPPED. Retain
+original first declaration/import evidence and no new aggregate/per-package PASS.
+
+The influence remains repository-wide: even a failed string in an unrelated
+environment may conservatively turn every remaining currently used, uncredited
+critical package's missing-pin WARNING into SKIPPED/INFO. The failed input can
+be supported by pip but outside this extractor; no assertion of a hidden exact
+pin or invalid file follows. Do not infer package use from the failed text.
+No-critical-use applicability and primary-Python empty-result veto stay intact;
+Python coverage does not control this existing declaration-failure branch.
+
+Keep thresholds, FAIL-only overrides, suppression, ordering and renderers.
+An isolated WARNING or promoted CRITICAL may cease causing exit 1; an independent
+qualifying finding can still cause exit 1. Default text may show PASS with a
+skipped count; default export removes that old warning/critical notable entry,
+while complete JSON retains the skipped finding and unrelated findings remain.
+Profiles, hints and init use the same captured inventory and remain unchanged.
+Do not reinterpret or rewrite historical audit/run/export records or snapshots.
+
+This continuation excludes Conda MatchSpec grammar, other manager package values,
+requirements graph/directive/continuation grammar, new dependency sources or
+installer execution, unknown/omitted use, candidate/listing/README/config/framework
+completeness and sufficient certificates. Do not change engine, scanner,
+redaction, persisted schemas, dependencies, version, historical gold or resource
+results. Wider R07-C remains OPEN.
 
